      "decision": "add_source_explicit_questions",
      "questions": [
        "先天性心脏病和认知障碍的遗传机制是什么？",
        "ETS-1在正常心脏发育中有何作用，其功能丧失如何导致先天性缺陷？"
      ],
      "questionEvidence": [
        {
          "questionIndex": 0,
          "sourceId": "src-93070f5ce1cdf232",
          "quote": "Using a combination of human and animal genetic model systems, our aim is to unravel the genetic mechanisms of congenital heart disease and cognitive disorders in order to develop improved therapies and ultimately, preventive strategies.",
          "quoteLocation": "body",
          "sourceObservedAt": "2026-10-16T01:02:55+00:00",
          "bodySha256": "e8de2f6d3e743686b1d53425a8d7379d268a501fb9210cb83919a7fa25bd5e6a",
          "sourceUrl": "https://pediatrics.ucsd.edu/research/faculty-labs/grossfeld-lab/index.html"
        },
        {
          "questionIndex": 1,
          "sourceId": "src-f5a4a5046618ec5a",
          "quote": "Using a combination of state-of-the art technologies including genetically engineered animal models and human induced pluripotent stem cells, Dr. Grossfeld’s laboratory is studying the function of the ETS-1 gene in normal heart development, and how loss of function causes congenital defects.",
          "quoteLocation": "body",
          "sourceObservedAt": "2026-10-16T01:33:50+00:00",
          "bodySha256": "58a92da893bb875edd48dd23c43668068a77bc63a84b95299973412908925f28",
          "sourceUrl": "https://pediatrics.ucsd.edu/research/faculty-labs/grossfeld-lab/about.html"
        }
      ],
      "reasonZh": "根页our aim与About具名laboratory明确求解遗传机制及ETS-1功能/缺失机制；原what we learn修辞仍排除，预防/治疗不表述为已证疗效。",
